PN,30902
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786384108
OL,3,CAnother heatwave on the way - is this
OL,4,Cbecoming the new normal?
OL,6,FIt will once again be a case of warm,
OL,7,Fstuffy nights offering little relief,
OL,8,Fwith temperatures struggling to fall
OL,9,Fenough for comfortable sleep.
OL,11,FThe difficulty now is finding new ways
OL,12,Fto describe what would once have been
OL,13,Fexceptional heat.
OL,15,FWe have lost count of the number of
OL,16,Fheatwaves this summer, with this
OL,17,Fmarking the fourth consecutive month
OL,18,Fwhere temperatures have reached 35C or
OL,19,Fabove.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30903
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F309A1786384108
OL,3,CAnother heatwave on the way - is this
OL,4,Cbecoming the new normal?
OL,6,FWhat was once a headline event is
OL,7,Fstarting to feel like a recurring
OL,8,Fpattern.
OL,10,FBut behind the familiar forecasts are
OL,11,Fbigger questions about how unusual
OL,12,Fthis summer really is, what it means
OL,13,Ffor our climate, and whether our
OL,14,Fperception of "extreme" heat is
OL,15,Fchanging.
OL,17,FAre these heatwaves no longer isolated
OL,18,Fevents, but part of a new summer
OL,19,Fpattern?
OL,26,@vD@OOUvD@WO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
